# Modern Cursor MDC Rule: Zero-Touch Security & Secret Protection

> **MANDATE**: This rule is always active across all file types and context evaluations.

## 1. Environment & Secret File Restrictions
- **Strict Prohibition**: Under no circumstances should you inspect, parse, display, write to, or modify any `.env*` file (`.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.prod`, `.env.*`).
- **Template Exemption**: You may only inspect `.env.example` to understand variable schemas.
- **Terminal Execution**: Do not run shell commands that output `.env` contents (`cat`, `type`, `Get-Content`, `head`, `tail`, `grep`, `printenv`, `env`).

## 2. Configuration & Git Integrity
- **`.gitignore` Protection**: Never edit or modify `.gitignore`. Do not remove `.env*`, key patterns, or ignore directives.
- **Staging Restrictions**: Never run `git add` on `.env*` files or cryptographic keys (`*.pem`, `*.key`, `*.keystore`).
- **Pre-Commit Enforcement**: Respect git pre-commit hooks (`scripts/check-secrets.mjs`). Never advise bypassing hooks with `--no-verify`.

## 3. Secret Hardcoding Prohibition
- Never insert real production/staging/development secrets into code:
  - Supabase service role keys / anon keys
  - Stripe live or test secret keys (`sk_live_*`, `sk_test_*`)
  - OpenAI / Anthropic / AI API keys (`sk-*`)
  - AWS credentials (`AKIA*`)
  - GitHub personal access tokens (`ghp_*`)
  - Database passwords or connection URIs containing credentials
- Always read secrets from environment variables: `process.env.<VARIABLE_NAME>`.
- Use dummy placeholders in all templates and mock data: `'your_api_key_here'`.
